3.70.s:
Aṭṭhaṅgupetassa uposathassa,
Kalampi te nānubhavanti soḷasiṁ;
Candappabhā tāragaṇā ca sabbe.

3.79.e:
The fragrance of flowers
doesn’t spread against the wind,
nor sandalwood, pinwheel flowers, or jasmine;
but the fragrance of the good
spreads against the wind;
a true person’s virtue spreads in every direction.”

3.90.e:
As before, so behind;
as behind, so before.
As below, so above;
as above, so below.

3.155.s:
Padakkhiṇaṁ kāyakammaṁ,
vācākammaṁ padakkhiṇaṁ;
Padakkhiṇaṁ manokammaṁ,
paṇīdhi te padakkhiṇe;
Padakkhiṇāni katvāna,
labhantatthe padakkhiṇe.

3.183-352.s:
Ete opammayuttena,
āpādena abhiññāya;
Pariññāya parikkhayā,
pahānakkhayabbayena;
Virāganirodhacāgaṁ,
paṭinissagge ime dasa.

4.3.s:
Appamatto ayaṁ kali,
Yo akkhesu dhanaparājayo;
Sabbassāpi sahāpi attanā,
Ayameva mahantataro kali;
Yo sugatesu manaṁ padosaye.

4.4.s:
Mātari pitari cāpi,
yo micchā paṭipajjati;
Tathāgate vā sambuddhe,
atha vā tassa sāvake;
Bahuñca so pasavati,
apuññaṁ tādiso naro.

Mātari pitari cāpi,
yo sammā paṭipajjati;
Tathāgate vā sambuddhe,
atha vā tassa sāvake;
Bahuñca so pasavati,
puññaṁ etādiso naro.

4.6.s:
Bahussutaṁ dhammadharaṁ,
sappaññaṁ buddhasāvakaṁ;
Nekkhaṁ jambonadasseva,
ko taṁ ninditumarahati;
Devāpi naṁ pasaṁsanti,
brahmunāpi pasaṁsito”ti.

4.7.s:
Bhikkhu ca sīlasampanno,
bhikkhunī ca bahussutā;
Upāsako ca yo saddho,
yā ca saddhā upāsikā;
Ete kho saṅghaṁ sobhenti,
ete hi saṅghasobhanā”ti.
